      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mathews County, where Hudgins lived, was named after the Speaker of the House who championed its creation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houlder_Hudgins_(Virginia)",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Battle of Gwynn's Island, a key early Revolutionary War clash, took place near Hudgins' home on July 8, 1776.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houlder_Hudgins_(Virginia)",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the war, Hudgins filed claims for a week's use of a boat, 55.5 pounds of bacon, two lambs, and 750 pounds of beef.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houlder_Hudgins_(Virginia)",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Donk's Theatre, once a local landmark in Hudgins, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2011.",
